      "explanation": "Given the equation,\n\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"12.177ex\" height=\"1.999ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -861.5 5382.2 883.5\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D44C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1040.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(2096.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D450\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D450\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(466,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D6FC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FC\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(3065.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"210E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-210E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(609,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D6FD\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FD\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(4129.3,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43A\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(819,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D6FE\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FE\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>\n\n<br><br>where Y represents Young's modulus, c the speed of light, h is Planck's constant, G is the gravitational constant, and α, β, and γ are powers to be determined. \n\n<br><br>We start by expressing the quantities involved in terms of their fundamental dimensions: Mass (M), Length (L), and Time (T). The equation in terms of dimensions is :\n\n<br><br><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-a